  "source_head_provenance": "ccb857cbc6d1745f589258b8b57e693123129462",
  "method": "One original treatment and macro path, two fresh full thirteen-year paths, each with independent policy clones of one pristine setup. The intervention replaces only the three Housing Benefit pension-age positive-entitlement passport predicates with pension-age actual Guarantee Credit receipt predicates; savings-credit-only branches remain unchanged and are recomputed normally. Fresh original and intervention household contributions supply all paired supports and complements. Household/person identity, age, pension type and weights are compared only in memory. Every linked count and monetary family is withheld together if any support or complement has one to nine records. HB effects have government-balance sign; other fiscal effects are the residual after HB. No survey identifier, weight, individual amount or unsafe numeric aggregate is written. This is an intervention sensitivity, not a statutory conclusion or a numerical-precision correction."
}
